          "level": "preferred",
          "summary": "Add affiliate/successor assignment freedom for the Company, a consent gate (and no-competitor limit) on HDI assignment, and confirm no HDI rights arise on a Company change of control.",
          "comment": "[Playbook] Section 10.3 currently binds successors and assigns but sets no consent standard, so HDI could transfer this hosting arrangement (including access to our data and Deerskin marks) to anyone, including a competitor. We have added our customary carve-out permitting the Company to assign to affiliates and M&A successors, a prior-written-consent requirement (not to be unreasonably withheld) on HDI assignments with no assignment to a Company competitor, and confirmation that a change of control of the Company gives HDI no termination or re-pricing right; if preferred, we can accept a mutual notice-plus-reasonable-consent formulation.",
          "ops": [
            {
              "kind": "replace",
              "paragraphId": "p0063",
              "oldText": "but no other person shall acquire or have any rights under this Agreement.",
              "newText": "but no other person shall acquire or have any rights under this Agreement. The Company may assign this Agreement, in whole or in part, without HDI's consent, to any affiliate of the Company or to any successor in connection with a merger, consolidation, reorganization, acquisition or sale of all or substantially all of its assets or of the business to which this Agreement relates, and neither any such assignment nor any change of control of the Company shall give HDI any right to terminate, suspend or re-price this Agreement. HDI may not assign or otherwise transfer this Agreement, in whole or in part, without the Company's prior written consent (which shall not be unreasonably withheld), and in no event to a competitor of the Company."
            }
          ]
        },
